   "t": 30.95,
   "kind": "thought",
   "data": {
    "text": "In `lagos-lekki-v3`, 120mm / 3h over the whole study area:\n\n### 1. Baseline vs lagoon held 1 m high\n\nBaseline `run_id: r_cf97d373df9a960d` vs tide-lock `run_id: r_ff5789b87fba8db6` with `tide boundary_level_m: 1.0`.\n\n> Tide here is the assumed lagoon/sea level from `get_aoi_info`, not a forecast. Default level is -0.5 m.\n\n| stat | baseline | 1 m lock | change alt-base |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| buildings_flooded | 26,114 | 26,527 | **+413 (+1.6%)** |\n| buildings_flooded_severe | 7,884 | 8,246 | **+362 (+4.6%)** |\n| people_exposed | 81,951 | 83,987 | +2,036 |\n| road_km_impassable | 353.548 km | 398.686 km | **+45.138 km (+12.8%)** |\n| flooded_area_km2 | 21.084 km2 | 27.740 km2 | **+6.656 km2 (+31.6%)** |\n| max_depth_m | 2.068 m | 2.089 m | +0.021 m |\n| peak_t_s | 10,200 | 10,200 | same timing |\n\nMechanism in the solver water balance:\n\n* `boundary_outflow_m3`: +1,514,071 to -4,821,059 — i.e. net inflow from the boundary under 1 m lock.\n* `stored_volume_end_m3`: 7,076,954 to 13,563,434 m3\n* `drained_volume_m3`: 626,339 to 422,215 m3\n* `drain_outfall_m3`: 215,153 to 40,693 m3\n* drain surcharge starts at 2,400 s baseline vs 600 s with lock, to 21,600 s in both.\n\nIn other words: tide lock does not change rain, but blocks outfall and holds water on the floodplain. Area floods much more than building count suggests — severe buildings and roads take most of the increase.\n\nLocal check at peak:\n\n* `area:Lekki Phase 1:buildings_flooded` 1,351 baseline vs 1,347 lock — essentially no change.\n* `area:Jakande:buildings_flooded` 1,437 baseline vs 1,441 lock — essentially no change.\n\nSo the +413 buildings study-wide is not concentrated in those two neighbourhoods.\n\n### 2. Evacuation route to nearest shelter\n\nTest from Jakande centroid `[3.50792, 6.42698]` at peak `t_s: 10200`:\n\n* Baseline: `route_id: rt_3363241818a6`, `reachable: false`, `edges_removed: 2360`\n* 1 m lock: `route_id: rt_bb2f794106c1`, `reachable: false`, `edges_removed: 2700`\n\nNo passable route to the nearest shelter at peak in either case, but the network is more degraded under lock — ~340 additional road edges removed as impassable.\n\nPlanning implication: for this storm, 1 m lagoon hold-up is primarily a road-accessibility and flood-extent problem (+45 km impassable, +6.66 km2) with a smaller but more severe building impact (+362 severe). Evacuation would need to occur before peak or via shelter-in-place planning, as peak-time movement from that origin is already cut off in the baseline and worse under lock.\n\nSolver is a planning model, not a forecast.\n"
   }
